From 65f73c33d6dd288d58d44ceb838f1ee193683f24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:27:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] draft(A6-41 item 3c): class-fields handoff on comma-list
 computed names

standard_decorators.rs: updated computed names keep the
GENERATED_COMPUTED_PROPERTY_NAME internal flag (the class-fields owners'
cache signal), and the class-name __setFunctionName of an explicitly named
class is requested after the members' helpers (it is a class-fields-pass
helper upstream, so __propKey precedes it at ES2015).
class_fields.rs (ES2022 set semantics): the lowered field key reuses the
cache assignment's generated binding found by find_computed_name_cache
(getGeneratedNameForNode(property.name) is the same generated name upstream)
instead of allocating a second binding.
class_fields/downlevel.rs (ES2015): the cache assignment is located through
find_computed_property_name_cache (parentheses and comma chains) instead of a
direct-assignment match.
---
 crates/emitter/src/builtins/class_fields.rs   | 40 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../src/builtins/class_fields/downlevel.rs    | 22 ++--------
 .../src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs       | 37 +++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

